  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF GUJARAT",
  "order": 2,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "a5ddt1r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient History of Gujarat"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Gujarat was home to key Indus Valley Civilization sites and early historical kingdoms.",
        "Medieval Gujarat witnessed successive rule under the Maitraka Dynasty (470–788 CE), Chaulukyas/Solankis (942–1244 CE), and Vaghela Dynasty (1244–1304 CE).",
        "The region came under Islamic rule through the Delhi Sultanate, later forming the independent Gujarat Sultanate (1407–1572 CE).",
        "Mughal control lasted from 1572 to 1758 CE before Maratha influence expanded across the region.",
        "British rule saw major princely states in Gujarat, an active participation in the Freedom Movement, and the eventual formation of Gujarat State."
      ],
      "id": "6636l4u"
    },
